      definition: "CSS colours can be written as **names** (`tomato`), **hex** (`#FF8A3D`), **rgb/rgba** (`rgb(255 138 61 / 0.5)`) or **hsl** (`hsl(24 100% 62%)`). **Background** properties set colours, images and gradients behind content. **Typography** properties \u2014 `font-family`, `font-size`, `font-weight`, `font-style`, `line-height`, `letter-spacing`, `text-align`, `text-transform` \u2014 control how text looks.",
      why: "Colour and type create the personality of a site and, more importantly, readability. Poor line-height or low contrast makes notes painful to read; good typography makes users stay.",
